  "files": {
    "Hi!": "2d8294845ec7.mp3",
    "I’m Ofek, and I’ll be your guide.": "3e1c2062aa28.mp3",
    "Welcome to the solar system!": "3d7408832ae4.mp3",
    "In the center is the Sun, and eight planets circle around it.": "6b9c37dea88b.mp3",
    "They all move around the Sun in the same direction, like race cars on a track, and almost on the same flat level, as if they were on a giant table.": "fbd480deb41d.mp3",
    "What keeps them on their path is the Sun’s gravity.": "fcd5faed0788.mp3",
    "The farther a planet is from the Sun, the slower it moves, and the longer its path is, so its year is longer too.": "07f2b385abc3.mp3",
    "The orbits are not perfect circles, but ellipses, like a circle that got a little squished.": "93bb96aa5a44.mp3",
    "When a planet gets closer to the Sun it speeds up, and when it moves away it slows down.": "3226bdec504b.mp3",
    "And all the planets are shown right where they are in the sky today!": "193745a908ea.mp3",
    "On top of that, every planet also spins around itself, like a spinning top.": "dd50d5f8b162.mp3",
    "Here’s a little secret: in real life the distances are much, much bigger.": "d2123d573731.mp3",
    "If we drew everything at its real size, the planets would be smaller than a dot and we couldn’t see them.": "0f1970982a14.mp3",
    "So here we made them bigger and moved them closer, so we can get to know all of them.": "37f3a5d3220c.mp3",
    "With the real distances button you can see how far away they really are.": "4310f00b2485.mp3",
    "Let’s go!": "a5998eba18f6.mp3",
    "This is the Sun!": "ce9e37012f06.mp3",
    "The Sun is a star, just like the stars we see at night, only much closer to us.": "5a8e5b030a04.mp3",
    "It is a giant ball of hot gas that lights up and warms the whole solar system.": "3b0cdfb1778a.mp3",
    "The Sun is so big that more than a million Earths could fit inside it.": "dbf549ac7e0c.mp3",
    "The Sun moves too!": "9cdb89d507f1.mp3",
    "It spins around itself, once every twenty-five days or so.": "723dd3ffa6db.mp3",
    "And since it is made of gas, its middle spins faster than the top and the bottom.": "7c1d6c05234f.mp3",
    "Here is another surprise: the Sun, along with all the planets, also zooms around the center of our galaxy, the Milky Way.": "6b060060553a.mp3",
    "One trip around takes about 230 million years!": "c5d18883f96d.mp3",
    "This is Mercury, the planet closest to the Sun, and also the smallest.": "8de7aec70411.mp3",
    "It is the fastest of them all: it circles the Sun in just eighty-eight days.": "58f663ad6cb1.mp3",
    "Its orbit is the most squished of all the planets, so sometimes it is closer to the Sun and sometimes farther away.": "225feb20dc84.mp3",
    "That means if you lived there, you would have a birthday almost four times a year!": "090074f65d2e.mp3",
    "But it spins around itself very slowly, so one day there is very long.": "b8e644a05dd6.mp3",
    "It has no air to hold in the heat, so by day it is hotter than an oven, and at night it is colder than any freezer.": "d4402cca7ed6.mp3",
    "This is Venus, the brightest thing in the night sky after the Moon.": "981afdaeac9f.mp3",
    "It is almost the same size as Earth, but it is the hottest planet in the solar system.": "67665f9fe5ad.mp3",
    "It is wrapped in thick clouds that trap the heat, like a very thick blanket, so it is even hotter there than on Mercury.": "5fefc48d02d5.mp3",
    "Venus has another oddity: it spins in the opposite direction from most planets, and very slowly.": "2f1944388781.mp3",
    "One spin takes longer than a whole trip around the Sun!": "73454c0ecb3f.mp3",
    "After the Moon, Venus is the brightest thing in the night sky, and sometimes it is called the morning star or the evening star.": "643bc96ee6dd.mp3",
    "And this is Earth, our home!": "64df6cdfcc84.mp3",
    "It is the only planet we know of that has life on it.": "4d035139ab9d.mp3",
    "Most of its surface is covered in water, so from space it looks blue.": "451115eeb2f9.mp3",
    "Earth spins around itself once a day, and that is how we get day and night.": "4664549454dc.mp3",
    "It goes around the Sun once a year.": "7c1d14cf9fd6.mp3",
