    "The directions and orbits are still like in real life, only the distances are smaller.": "f8f6029180f4.mp3",
    "Between Mars and Jupiter is the asteroid belt.": "77faf854fa4a.mp3",
    "Asteroids are rocks that go around the Sun.": "a1d8cfc69383.mp3",
    "Some are small as a pebble, and some are big as a mountain, or even as a city.": "c8548b13e4cf.mp3",
    "There are millions of asteroids there, but they are very far apart, so spacecraft fly through the belt without bumping into anything.": "3c5e3ac4111e.mp3",
    "The asteroids are leftovers from the time when the solar system was born: material that never managed to join into one planet, probably because of Jupiter’s strong gravity.": "8ef204235330.mp3",
    "The biggest object in the belt is Ceres, which is a dwarf planet, like Pluto.": "e715bb5e2896.mp3",
    "Here’s a surprising secret: the solar system is not standing still!": "09d5f7984144.mp3",
    "The Sun is zooming through space, and all the planets zoom along with it.": "116462223820.mp3",
    "Do you see the glowing tail behind the Sun?": "5254372fa23d.mp3",
    "It shows the path it travels as it flies forward.": "b325e27ab017.mp3",
    "It moves around the center of our galaxy, the Milky Way, at about two hundred and thirty kilometers every second!": "e9ad32bc943c.mp3",
    "One whole trip around the center of the galaxy takes about two hundred and thirty million years.": "6550ebc8826a.mp3",
    "Because the planets circle the Sun while it flies forward, their path through space is not a circle, but a spiral, like a stretched spring.": "cb75fc4c16f7.mp3",
