    "When it gets close to the Sun, its ice warms up and turns into gas, and the comet grows a glowing cloud and a long tail.": "c23c22ba7fb7.mp3",
    "A meteor is a tiny grain of dust or rock from space that zooms into Earth's air super fast and burns up.": "ff9a6882da4c.mp3",
    "From the ground it looks like a short streak of light in the sky, so people also call it a shooting star, even though it is not a star at all.": "c159443fbef9.mp3",
    "A meteor shower is a night when you can see lots of meteors like that.": "e179e1deca9c.mp3",
    "An ellipse is a shape like a circle that has been squashed a little, a bit like an egg lying on its side.": "f2684fde7ced.mp3",
    "The orbits of the planets are ellipses, so sometimes a planet is closer to the Sun, and sometimes it is farther away.": "6e0c6b84c05d.mp3",
    "A black hole is a place in space where gravity is so strong that nothing can escape from it, not even light.": "c5bd1680d4fd.mp3",
    "Black holes form when a giant star runs out of fuel and collapses in on itself.": "4777cb12108e.mp3",
    "They do not gobble up everything in space, like many people think.": "10dd88d4dcf7.mp3",
    "If a black hole with the same weight as our Sun took its place, Earth would keep going around it just like now.": "3e6402370acd.mp3",
    "Only something that gets very, very close can never come back.": "8dec6455ea4e.mp3",
    "Light is the fastest thing there is.": "c9faf119778d.mp3",
    "It travels almost three hundred thousand kilometers every second!": "6e17dca14fc4.mp3",
    "A light-year is the distance light travels in one whole year, which is about nine and a half trillion kilometers.": "d4e14619c909.mp3",
    "We use it to measure distances between stars, because they are so far away that the numbers in kilometers would be way too long.": "2eb6d4537637.mp3",
    "When we say a star is ten light-years away, it means its light travels for ten years before it reaches us.": "446fc451c5df.mp3",
    "Mass is the amount of stuff that is inside an object.": "e61c1bd542cb.mp3",
    "The more stuff an object has, the bigger its mass, and the stronger its gravity.": "50a4fdf7ea50.mp3",
    "When we say a black hole is ten times heavier than the Sun, it means its mass is ten times the mass of the Sun.": "a9b5ccb871e6.mp3",
    "When gas falls toward a black hole, it does not fall straight in.": "6e8498f1d6d8.mp3",
    "It swirls around it at a crazy speed, like water swirling around the drain in a bathtub.": "eacca90b3339.mp3",
    "With all that speed and rubbing, the gas heats up until it is burning hot and glowing, and that makes a shining ring.": "a44d5a7ae7b9.mp3",
    "The black hole itself stays black, but the ring around it glows.": "5f92ab500fdf.mp3",
    "Strong gravity does not only pull on things, it also bends the path of light.": "5d5f9e491547.mp3",
    "Light that passes near a black hole curves around it, like a car going around a bend.": "97657e85a20a.mp3",
    "That is why, when you look at a black hole, the stars behind it look stretched and flipped, and you can even see the same ring both above and below it.": "a9cca32d3fd4.mp3",
    "Andromeda is the biggest galaxy that is close to the Milky Way.": "b42fe67c1d32.mp3",
    "It is about two and a half million light-years away from us.": "17fb1f6cf263.mp3",
    "It has about a trillion stars, more than our own Milky Way.": "f419c3e22180.mp3",
    "On a very dark night, far from city lights, you can see it with your own eyes, as a small, fuzzy patch of light in the sky.": "1d8f757fa94b.mp3",
    "It is one of the farthest things you can see without a telescope!": "2a7ede540677.mp3",
    "Want me to keep explaining?": "369a930801ef.mp3",
    "The Moon is our closest neighbor in space.": "4f84f06058fb.mp3",
    "It goes around Earth once about every month, and it always shows us the same side.": "bb78d456b0d4.mp3",
    "The Moon does not make its own light.": "078061c65a56.mp3",
    "It bounces back the light of the Sun, so it looks different to us.": "d3a38f817ff1.mp3",
    "Sometimes it is full, sometimes half, and sometimes just a thin sliver.": "f1085f78ec68.mp3",
    "Those are the phases of the Moon.": "5e20bbdb2101.mp3",
    "The Moon has no air and no flowing water, and it is covered with craters, which are holes made when space rocks crashed into it.": "3dc38cd1415f.mp3",
    "In 1969 the first person walked on the Moon, and so far only twelve people have ever walked there.": "db983f29901e.mp3",
    "Phobos is the bigger of the two moons of Mars, but it is still very small, only about as big as a city.": "b09c8998e4b9.mp3",
    "Its shape is not round.": "871fe0887a2c.mp3",
    "It looks like a potato!": "4a460c2a0f74.mp3",
    "Phobos is so close to Mars that it goes around it three times every day!": "ae3702622476.mp3",
    "And it is slowly getting closer to Mars, so in tens of millions of years it will break apart or crash into the planet.": "2a9450ac2720.mp3",
    "Deimos is the smaller moon of Mars, and it is farther away.": "2e2b599a6f87.mp3",
    "It is shaped like a potato too!": "6a326b1db255.mp3",
    "Its gravity is very weak, so a kid who jumped on it would float up for a really long time before landing.": "c81acc868d41.mp3",
    "From the ground of Mars, Deimos looks like a bright star, not like a moon.": "c42eb093a5af.mp3",
    "Io is the most explosive moon in the solar system!": "fa15da1ba95d.mp3",
    "It has hundreds of active volcanoes that shoot yellow and orange sulfur high into space.": "8fbc3e61d3f0.mp3",
    "That is why it looks like a colorful pizza.": "df8fd89822ec.mp3",
    "The gravity of Jupiter keeps squeezing and stretching Io, like a ball of dough, and that heats up its tummy.": "a2fb97ea85db.mp3",
    "Europa is covered with a thick layer of ice, and hiding under the ice is a giant ocean of salty water, with more water than all the oceans on Earth put together!": "5de638bf5d10.mp3",
    "Scientists think there might be tiny living things there, so a special spacecraft was sent to explore it.": "ec1b7deb5350.mp3",
    "Ganymede is the biggest moon in the solar system.": "50688a347d86.mp3",
    "It is even bigger than the planet Mercury!": "7a44723f64e0.mp3",
    "It is the only moon with a magnetic field of its own, like a giant magnet, and an ocean is probably hiding under its ice.": "11d8bfcd3622.mp3",
    "Callisto is one of the most crater-covered places in the solar system.": "53d64e97ff40.mp3",
    "Its surface has hardly changed for billions of years, so it is like a history book of all the rocks that crashed into it from space.": "772b7473755d.mp3",
    "Enceladus is a small, white moon like a snowball, and one of the brightest things in the solar system.": "cebac60b42f0.mp3",
    "Giant fountains of water and ice burst into space from its south pole, just like geysers.": "b2268b2dec16.mp3",
    "Under the ice there is an ocean, and scientists think it might have just the right conditions for life.": "a317d6a826ed.mp3",
    "Titan is the big moon of Saturn, and the only moon with a thick atmosphere, even thicker than the atmosphere of Earth.": "5729a4526fe6.mp3",
    "It has lakes and rivers, but they are not made of water.": "82c29302777e.mp3",
    "They are made of liquid methane, because it is really, really cold there.": "be5da32c4c62.mp3",
    "A spacecraft called Huygens already landed on Titan, and in the next few years a flying drone called Dragonfly is supposed to fly there.": "50eccf4e5ccc.mp3",
    "Miranda is a small moon of Uranus, with the strangest face of all.": "1533c56d44b5.mp3",
    "It looks like it was glued together from different pieces, like a puzzle.": "164ad63b67a2.mp3",
    "It has a giant cliff about twenty kilometers tall, more than twice as tall as Mount Everest!": "6dc39e1893b4.mp3",
    "Titania is the biggest moon of Uranus, and it is made of about half ice and half rock.": "c8ee6f851d14.mp3",
    "The moons of Uranus are named after characters in plays by the famous writer Shakespeare, and Titania is the queen of the fairies in one of his plays.": "a9d491aafc66.mp3",
    "Triton is the big moon of Neptune, and it goes around the planet in the opposite direction, unlike all the other big moons in the solar system.": "39e36ba2c8d5.mp3",
    "It was probably once a loner wandering through space, until Neptune caught it with its gravity.": "66f3b134ac21.mp3",
    "Triton is one of the coldest places ever measured, and it has geysers that shoot out nitrogen gas.": "7f8ff61361f7.mp3",
    "Charon is the big moon of Pluto, and it is almost half as big as Pluto itself!": "db7e3f081117.mp3",
    "Pluto and Charon always show each other the same side, as if they were dancing together and holding hands.": "9377de73124a.mp3",
    "At the north pole of Charon there is a reddish patch nicknamed Mordor, after the land in the story The Lord of the Rings.": "777ed41c1eaa.mp3",
    "Comets are like giant, dirty snowballs: lumps of ice, dust, and rock that come from the far edges of the solar system.": "81879a3795e5.mp3",
    "Most of the time they are frozen and dark.": "856c523993a3.mp3",
    "But when a comet gets close to the Sun, the heat warms it up, and its ice turns into gas.": "59e650d95d48.mp3",
    "A glowing cloud forms around it, and long tails stretch out behind it.": "9d8ec90ba8f9.mp3",
    "A comet has two tails.": "1fedc0d34f83.mp3",
    "One is a bluish tail of gas that always points away from the Sun, and the other is a yellowish tail of dust that curves a little.": "316cc44c6cf2.mp3",
    "The tail can be longer than the distance between Earth and the Sun!": "854dbdc7a1e2.mp3",
    "The orbits of comets are very squashed.": "10ce5c4635f0.mp3",
    "They swoop really close to the Sun, and then they travel far, far away from it.": "c0a5f5d953e7.mp3",
    "This is Halley's Comet, the most famous comet of all.": "6e540fa8fbc9.mp3",
    "It comes back to our sky about once every seventy-five years, so most people see it only once in their lives.": "2374accd126d.mp3",
    "The last time it came was in 1986, and the next time it will come is in 2061.": "dbdc7a662b67.mp3",
    "Maybe you will see it when you grow up!": "b2b23c00b7a6.mp3",
    "Halley's Comet goes around the Sun in the opposite direction from the planets.": "ef78f1208e1c.mp3",
    "Right now it is very far away, even beyond the orbit of Neptune, so it has no tail at all.": "ab6a7dc22d94.mp3",
    "This is Encke's Comet.": "b77cb0fe9c8c.mp3",
    "It has one of the shortest orbits of any comet.": "00ae8769f67e.mp3",
    "It goes around the Sun in only three years and three months.": "0a60a03718bc.mp3",
    "It is small and faint, so it is hard to see without a telescope.": "3f060f533a80.mp3",
    "When it comes close to the Sun, it gets even closer than the planet Mercury!": "f3ce863303ce.mp3",
    "And the dust it leaves behind causes a meteor shower every fall.": "dd742be9b4b8.mp3",
    "This comet has a long name, Churyumov-Gerasimenko, or just 67P for short.": "f0e098432250.mp3",
    "It is famous because in 2014 the spacecraft Rosetta arrived there, flew alongside it for two years, and even landed a little robot on it, called Philae.": "7b60811631c2.mp3",
    "It was the first time people ever landed anything on a comet!": "1d2ea5387311.mp3",
    "And in the pictures Rosetta took, we could see that its shape looks like a rubber duck.": "bdf808ebfae5.mp3"
  }
}
